<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">India</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">India is a region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>, home to some of the world's oldest civilisations and a long series of empires, including the Maurya, Gupta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, Mughal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> states. Its wealth and trade drew the attention of many outside powers. It was invaded by the Macedonian and Timurid empires and became the centrepiece of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/india.jpg" alt="India" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
